  p("pcm-set-u5-01","U5","5.6","Newton's Second Law in Rotational Form","2.B","What rotational inertia is implied by the data?",["0.5 kg m^2","2 kg m^2","4 kg m^2","8 kg m^2"],1,"For each row τ/α=2 kg m^2. Since τ=I α, the rotor's rotational inertia is 2 kg m^2. The same ratio in every trial independently supports one fixed rotational inertia for the rotor.",{stimulusGroupId:"pcm-set-u5",stimulus:PCM_SET_U5});
  p("pcm-set-u5-02","U5","5.6","Newton's Second Law in Rotational Form","3.C","Which observation supports treating the rotational inertia as constant?",["Torque is always positive","The ratio τ/α is constant","Angular acceleration is nonzero","The largest torque occurs last"],1,"A constant value of τ/α across all trials means the proportionality constant I in τ=I α remains unchanged.",{stimulusGroupId:"pcm-set-u5",stimulus:PCM_SET_U5});
